{
  "text": "Malcolm, let us talk about mastery. People took the 10,000 hour rule as a promise of guaranteed genius. The reality is that practice is a necessary condition, but never a sufficient one. What matters far more is deliberate practice under ruthless feedback. Mindless repetition simply ingrains your existing mistakes deeper. The great performers seek out friction every single training session. That is what separates the elite from the merely experienced. Early specialization traps young athletes in narrow movement patterns. Sampling a wide variety of domains builds adaptive resilience. Generalists thrive in complex, unpredictable environments.",
